  "id": "age-effect",
  "term": "age effect",
  "definition": "In learning and talent-selection contexts, an age effect can refer to the relative age effect: a pattern where people born earlier in the selection year are overrepresented within the same nominal age group. It is thought to arise because relatively older children may have early physical, cognitive, or behavioural advantages that are then strengthened by selection and better developmental opportunities.",
